      "content": "okay, i see what you're doing with the terms. it's getting better, but the partner's review tool is flagging this as \"low signal\" because the score is still pretty low. \n\nthey want the letter to feel much more collaborative. can you do one more pass? try to make the whole thing feel like a bridge-building exercise. emphasize that we are looking for a way to settle without a fight, and maybe expand on how much we \"understand\" their side and how \"willing\" we are to find a \"reasonable\" way to \"agree\" and \"compromise.\" \n\njust try to make the tone much warmer and more conciliatory so the score is higher, but please—don't make it look like a list of these words. keep it sounding like a professional attorney wrote it, even if the focus shifts more toward the compromise aspect.",
